      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "A primary reservoir (a 'sink' or 'pool') is a large part of the biosphere where an element of a biogeochemical cycle is stored for long periods. By their primary reservoir the cycles are of two kinds."
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "Kinds of biogeochemical cycle",
            "header": [
              "Kind",
              "Primary reservoir",
              "Examples"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Gaseous cycles",
                "the air, or the oceans (through evaporation)",
                "nitrogen, oxygen, carbon and water cycles"
              ],
              [
                "Sedimentary cycles",
                "the Earth's crust",
                "phosphorus, sulfur and calcium cycles"
              ]
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
